│ patch_description        │ Replace the highly overparameterized seed with a three-parameter, symmetry-tied ansatz.   │
│                          │ Global RY and RZ layers learn a common measurement basis, while shared XX interactions on │
│                          │ a ring and across opposite qubits provide local and long-range correlation mixing without │
│                          │ adding parameters. Repeating this noncommuting block three times yields useful            │
│                          │ expressivity while preserving a strong permutation/translation-inspired inductive bias.   │
│                          │ This reduces circuit parameters from 24 to 3 (5 including gain and bias), which should    │
│                          │ reduce few-shot overfitting, improve parameter efficiency, and make optimization faster   │
│                          │ and more stable.                                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
