│ patch_description        │ Replace the independently parameterized hardware-efficient circuit with a                 │
│                          │ translation-invariant, three-parameter Floquet/quantum-convolution block. A shared global │
│                          │ RY field, shared periodic ZZ interaction, and shared global RX field form a noncommuting  │
│                          │ transverse-Ising layer. Repeating this tied block three times spreads two-qubit           │
│                          │ information into the fixed correlator readout while retaining a strong symmetry prior.    │
│                          │ Closing the interaction ring removes boundary-specific behavior, and sharing each         │
│                          │ parameter across all eight qubits sharply reduces few-shot overfitting and the circuit    │
│                          │ parameter count from 24 to 3 (5 including gain and bias), improving parameter efficiency  │
