│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ collective_ising_qaoa                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed-strength CZ circuit and three rotation parameters with a                │
│                          │ translationally symmetric, two-parameter QAOA-style block. One shared RY parameter learns │
│                          │ a collective measurement basis, while one shared ZZ parameter continuously tunes          │
│                          │ correlation processing across the periodic nearest-neighbor graph. Repeating this same    │
│                          │ noncommuting mixer–interaction block three times provides useful nonlinear expressivity   │
│                          │ without qubit-specific parameters. This reduces the circuit parameter count from three to │
│                          │ two, improves regularization and parameter efficiency, and allows training to suppress    │
│                          │ unnecessary entanglement rather than being forced through a maximal CZ layer.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
