│ patch_name               │ tied_kicked_ising                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the fixed-CZ Euler architecture with a translation-symmetric kicked-Ising block. │
│                          │ Each block alternates even-ring ZZ interactions, a collective RX mixer, and odd-ring ZZ   │
│                          │ interactions. Every gate shares one angle, reducing the circuit to one trainable quantum  │
│                          │ parameter (three total including gain and bias). The trainable entanglers can             │
│                          │ continuously recover the identity, while the noncommuting interaction/mixer sequence      │
│                          │ propagates pair information across the ring over the three fixed repetitions. This        │
│                          │ provides a strong low-capacity inductive bias for few-shot generalization, lowers circuit │
│                          │ depth and gate count, and makes optimization substantially simpler.                       │
