│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ readout_floquet_mixer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces the hardware-efficient ring circuit with a readout-aligned,                 │
│                          │ Hamiltonian-inspired Floquet mixer. Every trainable gate shares one angle, leaving only   │
│                          │ one circuit parameter plus the fixed gain and bias. A collective RY layer changes the     │
│                          │ local measurement basis, while shared XX and reverse-ordered ZZ interactions act directly │
│                          │ on the dataset-supplied readout graph. Because these generators do not generally commute  │
│                          │ on overlapping pairs, the three tied repetitions still produce a nonlinear correlated     │
│                          │ transformation rather than merely tripling one rotation.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach should generalize better in the few-shot regime because it uses the readout  │
│                          │ topology as an inductive bias, avoids qubit-specific parameters, and reduces optimization │
│                          │ to a stable one-dimensional circuit search. It also improves parameter efficiency from    │
│                          │ five total parameters to three while retaining entangling capacity for difficult          │
│                          │ validation groups.                                                                        │
