│ patch_name               │ even_odd_euler                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace fully collective rotations with a semi-collective even/odd Euler pattern. The     │
│                          │ current ansatz forces all eight qubits into the same learned basis and performs poorly,   │
│                          │ indicating excessive symmetry and underfitting. Tying parameters within parity groups     │
│                          │ preserves strong few-shot regularization while allowing two distinct local bases, which   │
│                          │ can capture staggered or sublattice structure and improve the hardest-group margin. The   │
│                          │ RZ-RY-RZ sequence supplies complete single-qubit basis control for each group, while      │
│                          │ sharing keeps the circuit to six distinct quantum parameters despite 24 gates and three   │
│                          │ repeated blocks.                                                                          │
