│ patch_description        │ Replace the dense XX Möbius layer with a translation-symmetric collective RZ→RY→RZ        │
│                          │ transformation followed by a nearest-neighbour ZZ ring. The two RZ layers share one       │
│                          │ parameter, while all ZZ interactions share one parameter, so the circuit retains only     │
│                          │ three distinct circuit parameters and does not worsen parameter efficiency. The           │
│                          │ palindromic collective rotations provide a richer measurement-basis transformation than   │
│                          │ the current single-sided RY/RZ layers, while the ZZ ring supplies controllable            │
│                          │ entanglement aligned with two-qubit correlation readout. Removing the four long-range     │
│                          │ interactions also reduces unnecessary few-shot capacity and should improve worst-group    │
│                          │ robustness and the train-test gap.                                                        │
