│ patch_name               │ hypercube_axis_mixer                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz retains the strongest lesson from the prior results—global parameter sharing  │
│                          │ and parameter-free entanglement—but replaces the Möbius ladder and trainable Ising        │
│                          │ network with a distinct interleaved hypercube construction. Three disjoint CZ matchings   │
│                          │ connect qubits according to the three bit-flip dimensions of a 3-dimensional hypercube,   │
│                          │ giving diameter-three information propagation aligned with the fixed three block          │
│                          │ repetitions.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead of placing all entanglers in one commuting layer, the matchings are separated by  │
│                          │ collective noncommuting RY, RZ, and RX rotations. RY and RX share one mixer parameter,    │
│                          │ while RZ uses one phase parameter, leaving only two circuit parameters and four total     │
│                          │ trainable parameters including readout calibration. This preserves parameter economy      │
│                          │ while producing richer repeated dynamics, balanced connectivity, and strong               │
│                          │ symmetry-based regularization for few-shot generalization.                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
