│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_nonlocal_ising                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the underperforming two-parameter hypercube circuit with a one-parameter Möbius   │
│                          │ ansatz that combines a collective RY basis change, a symmetric CZ ring, and shared        │
│                          │ IsingXX rotations across antipodal pairs. The trainable nonlocal interactions directly    │
│                          │ adapt four long-range correlations that fixed CZ gates can only phase, while the ring     │
│                          │ distributes those features across all wires over the three tied repetitions. Sharing the  │
│                          │ same angle across every rotation and interaction constrains the model to a strongly       │
│                          │ regularized one-dimensional trajectory, reducing the total parameter count from four to   │
│                          │ three including readout calibration. This should improve few-shot generalization and      │
│                          │ parameter efficiency while retaining noncommuting, globally connected dynamics for        │
│                          │ hard-group separation.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
