│ patch_name               │ tunable_mobius_chords                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the underperforming readout-graph Floquet circuit with the previously stronger    │
│                          │ symmetry-regularized Möbius-ladder structure. A single collective angle remains shared by │
│                          │ every RY and RZ rotation, preserving parameter economy and few-shot generalization. The   │
│                          │ local ring uses fixed CZ gates, while the four diametric Möbius chords use one shared ZZ  │
│                          │ parameter. This adds only one circuit degree of freedom but allows optimization to        │
│                          │ control non-local correlation strength independently, which should improve worst-group    │
│                          │ separation without introducing wire-specific parameters or excessive training capacity.   │
