│ patch_name               │ hybrid_mobius_entangler                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Preserve the current one-parameter economy while making the fixed entangler more          │
│                          │ expressive. The commuting CZ ring retains a regular, low-overfitting inductive bias,      │
│                          │ while replacing only the four diametric CZ gates with disjoint CNOTs introduces           │
│                          │ non-diagonal long-range information transport. This hybrid Clifford topology can spread   │
│                          │ difficult global correlations into the fixed two-qubit readout more effectively than an   │
│                          │ entirely diagonal CZ network, without adding parameters or gates. It avoids the score     │
│                          │ penalty observed when splitting the collective angle into two parameters.                 │
