│ patch_description        │ Add a translation-symmetric ring of distance-three CZ couplings to the existing Möbius    │
│                          │ ladder. The current one-parameter circuit generalizes well but has a weaker worst-group   │
│                          │ margin, suggesting that its fixed correlation graph may not propagate some difficult      │
│                          │ nonlocal features sufficiently. These additional parameter-free links complement the      │
│                          │ nearest-neighbour and antipodal edges, reduce correlation bottlenecks, and preserve the   │
│                          │ strong dihedral symmetry and single trainable circuit parameter that support few-shot     │
│                          │ generalization and parameter efficiency.                                                  │
