│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the inspiration program’s minimum one-parameter circuit while        │
│                          │ retaining the current program’s trainable correlation processing. A single shared angle   │
│                          │ drives both the collective RY mixer and the nearest-neighbour ZZ ring, giving only three  │
│                          │ total parameters including readout gain and bias. The fixed Möbius CZ network preserves   │
│                          │ broad local and long-range connectivity. Removing the separate RZ layer keeps the block   │
│                          │ at 28 gates, matching the lower-gate inspiration candidate while replacing local phase    │
│                          │ processing with correlation-sensitive ZZ rotations that may improve hard-group            │
│                          │ separation.                                                                               │
