│                          │ existing global_y parameter. This keeps the circuit at two distinct ansatz parameters—the │
│                          │ same count as the current candidate—while reallocating one degree of freedom from a       │
│                          │ redundant independent global rotation to direct control of long-range entanglement. The   │
│                          │ shared cross-chord angle preserves permutation-like regularization, can adapt the         │
│                          │ strength and sign of all nonlocal correlations coherently, and may improve the            │
│                          │ hardest-group margin without increasing parameter cost or encouraging wire-specific       │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
