│ patch_name               │ tied_mobius_zz                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the weaker two-parameter local-rotation ansatz with a single-parameter            │
│                          │ correlation ansatz based on the strongest prior candidate. The collective angle is shared │
│                          │ by every RY and ZZ gate, reducing the total parameter count from four to three while      │
│                          │ preserving a trainable noncommuting mixer. Extending the proven nearest-neighbour ZZ ring │
│                          │ onto the four diametric Möbius chords makes long-range correlations trainable without     │
│                          │ adding parameters. This symmetry-preserving inductive bias should improve hard-group      │
│                          │ separation while limiting few-shot overfitting.                                           │
