│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ readout_aligned_shared_crz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current circuit uses two distinct circuit angles, producing four total trainable      │
│                          │ parameters after gain and bias, while the strongest prior result used only one circuit    │
│                          │ angle. The proposed ansatz returns to one distinct circuit parameter and therefore three  │
│                          │ total parameters. It retains the successful collective RY mixer, fixed Möbius CZ graph,   │
│                          │ and shared nearest-neighbour ZZ layer, then adds dataset-aligned CRZ gates on the fixed   │
│                          │ readout pairs. These CRZ gates reuse the same collective angle, adding targeted control   │
│                          │ over the correlations ultimately measured without increasing parameter count. This        │
│                          │ stronger structural bias should improve worst-group separation and few-shot               │
│                          │ generalization while avoiding the extra local parameter and tied terminal RZ layer that   │
│                          │ reduced the current score. Fixed Adam settings—learning rate 0.03, 1000 epochs, 30 steps  │
│                          │ per epoch, batch size 15, validation-loss selection, and patience 75—remain unchanged as  │
│                          │ required.                                                                                 │
