│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ readout_aligned_crz                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This design replaces the generic dense CZ connectivity with a sparse, measurement-aligned │
│                          │ circuit. A globally shared RY mixer provides a regularized basis change, while shared CRZ │
│                          │ gates act directly on the dataset-supplied readout pairs. Because the CRZ layer ends      │
│                          │ every block, it is also the final trainable operation before measurement after the third  │
│                          │ repetition. This focuses the single circuit parameter on correlations that directly       │
│                          │ affect the fixed observable, reduces unnecessary depth and gate count, and preserves the  │
│                          │ three-total-parameter economy that performed best in prior candidates.                    │
