│ patch_name               │ shared_correlation_readout                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the weaker collective RZ trajectory with the previously stronger shared ZZ ring,  │
│                          │ while retaining the readout-aligned CRZ layer. Crucially, the CRZ gates now reuse the     │
│                          │ same collective parameter instead of introducing a second circuit parameter. This         │
│                          │ combines correlation-sensitive processing with readout-pair adaptation while reducing the │
│                          │ model from two distinct circuit parameters to one, improving few-shot regularization and  │
│                          │ parameter efficiency. The terminal CRZ placement also makes it the closest                │
│                          │ schema-compatible approximation to a shared readout-phase layer without modifying the     │
│                          │ fixed circuit or measurement code.                                                        │
