│ patch_description        │ Replace the underperforming second collective single-qubit mixer and shifted CZ matching  │
│                          │ with tied nearest-neighbor ZZ and YY correlation layers. The prior results show that      │
│                          │ shared ZZ correlations generalize substantially better than the current RX/CZ tail.       │
│                          │ Adding the orthogonal YY layer increases access to noncommuting correlation features that │
│                          │ can improve the hardest-group margin, while reusing `collective_angle` preserves the      │
│                          │ minimum one-dimensional circuit parameterization and its strong few-shot regularization.  │
