│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ decoupled_mobius_angles                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the underperforming chord-only trainable layer and tied terminal RZ rotations     │
│                          │ with the stronger prior Möbius topology: collective RY mixing, a fixed CZ ring plus       │
│                          │ diametric chords, and trainable ZZ correlations on the ring. The mixer and correlation    │
│                          │ layers receive separate global angles, allowing Adam to tune basis selection              │
│                          │ independently from correlation strength while retaining cyclic symmetry and only two      │
│                          │ circuit parameters. This keeps the current parameter count and gate count unchanged but   │
│                          │ uses them more effectively, removes the potentially restrictive RY/RZ parameter tying,    │
│                          │ and restores the topology associated with better validation and worst-group margins.      │
