│ patch_name               │ tied_orthogonal_ising_ring                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This design keeps the strongest observed inductive biases: a collective basis rotation,   │
│                          │ parameter-free Möbius connectivity, and strict translation symmetry. It removes the       │
│                          │ current ansatz’s second circuit parameter, restoring the three-total-parameter economy of │
│                          │ the best prior candidates. The novel component is an edgewise interleaving of tied ZZ and │
│                          │ YY interactions. Each YY gate immediately follows its corresponding ZZ gate and shares    │
│                          │ the same collective angle used by every other parametrized gate. This adds orthogonal     │
│                          │ correlation channels at zero parameter cost, while overlapping ring edges and repeated    │
│                          │ collective RY layers generate noncommuting dynamics. The resulting one-dimensional        │
│                          │ circuit trajectory should regularize few-shot training while offering richer correlator   │
│                          │ transformation for the hardest validation groups.                                         │
