│ patch_name               │ tied_zy_correlation_ladder                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz replaces the underperforming pair of collective RX/RY mixers with a           │
│                          │ symmetry-regularized correlation processor. A shared RY basis change is followed by a     │
│                          │ parameter-free Möbius CZ network, then interleaved ZZ and YY rotations on every ring      │
│                          │ edge. The orthogonal Ising channels generate noncommuting correlations across adjacent    │
│                          │ edges, increasing useful expressivity while retaining only one distinct circuit           │
│                          │ parameter. This preserves strong parameter efficiency and few-shot regularization while   │
│                          │ targeting harder validation groups through richer two-qubit correlation transport.        │
