│ patch_description        │ Give all readout-aligned CRZ gates one shared parameter that is independent of the        │
│                          │ collective RY/ZZ angle. The current tying forces basis mixing, correlation evolution, and │
│                          │ measurement-aligned phase adjustment to use the same value despite representing different │
│                          │ generators. A dedicated phase can improve the hardest-group margin by rotating            │
│                          │ correlations specifically toward the supplied readout observable. Sharing it across every │
│                          │ readout pair preserves symmetry and adds only one trainable scalar, limiting overfitting  │
│                          │ in the few-shot regime.                                                                   │
