│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tied_zz_yy_mobius                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses two circuit angles (`global_y`, `global_z`), giving four total    │
│                          │ trainable parameters after gain and bias, yet reaches only 0.77 validation accuracy. The  │
│                          │ strongest prior structure instead used one shared circuit angle and achieved 0.82         │
│                          │ validation accuracy with better parameter efficiency.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This proposal restores that one-angle regularization and retains the Möbius CZ network,   │
│                          │ shared RY basis mixing, ring ZZ correlations, and readout-aligned CRZ gates. It           │
│                          │ additionally inserts an IsingYY gate immediately after every IsingZZ gate, using the same │
│                          │ shared angle. The orthogonal YY channel broadens correlation processing without adding    │
│                          │ trainable parameters, which should improve difficult-group separation while preserving    │
│                          │ few-shot generalization. The fixed Adam settings—learning rate 0.03, 1000 epochs, 30      │
│                          │ steps per epoch, batch size 15, validation-loss early stopping with patience 75—remain    │
│                          │ unchanged. The model has one circuit parameter and three total parameters including       │
│                          │ readout gain and bias.                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.2591                                                                                   │
