│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ shared_yz_mobius                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover retains the stronger one-parameter correlation architecture—collective RY  │
│                          │ mixing, Möbius CZ connectivity, shared ZZ processing, and readout-aligned CRZ gates—while │
│                          │ adding the collective RZ basis layer from the lower-depth parent. The RZ gates reuse the  │
│                          │ same scalar, so the circuit still has only one distinct circuit parameter and three total │
│                          │ trainable parameters including gain and bias. Because the diagonal correlation layer is   │
│                          │ followed by a shared RZ rotation before the next repeated RY layer, the three tied        │
│                          │ repetitions alternate noncommuting collective basis changes and correlation processing,   │
│                          │ increasing the useful one-dimensional feature family without weakening parameter economy. │
