│ patch_description        │ Decouple nearest-neighbor and opposite-wire correlation scales while preserving strong    │
│                          │ symmetry-based parameter sharing. The ring ZZ gates receive one shared local parameter,   │
│                          │ while four Möbius cross-chord ZZ gates retain the collective parameter already used by    │
│                          │ the global RY layer. This replaces the redundant same-edge YY interactions with explicit  │
│                          │ long-range correlations, keeps the model compact at only two circuit parameters, lowers   │
│                          │ gate count, and should improve worst-group separation by allowing short- and long-range   │
│                          │ structure to be optimized independently.                                                  │
