│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ readout_aligned_mobius                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the four trainable diametric ZZ rotations with directional CRZ rotations on the   │
│                          │ dataset-supplied readout pairs. The current diametric ZZ terms reuse interactions already │
│                          │ represented by the fixed Möbius chords and appear to reduce validation and worst-group    │
│                          │ margins. Readout-aligned CRZ gates instead transform the exact pair features consumed by  │
│                          │ the classifier and introduce useful noncommuting, directional structure. All gates retain │
│                          │ the single shared angle, so the candidate remains at one circuit parameter and three      │
│                          │ total trainable parameters while recovering the stronger regularized structure seen in    │
│                          │ prior results.                                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1612                                                                                   │
